1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:06,423
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:08,174
[STAFF MEMBER]
<i>We'll turn her over to you, ma'am.</i>

3
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:09,426
[OFFICER]<i> Okay.</i>

4
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:13,346
[GUN CLICKS]

5
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:16,099
<i>Don't fight back. Give me your gun.</i>

6
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:19,728
<i>Hurry!</i>

7
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:26,776
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

8
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:30,155
[CALOY] <i>Move.</i>

9
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:32,949
<i>This way.</i>

10
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,456
<i>Sir?</i>

11
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:42,041
[BILLY GASPS]

12
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:42,959
<i>Billy.</i>

13
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:47,422
- [LOUD THWACK]
- [MARIELA YELPS]

14
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:49,466
- [MARIELA SHRIEKS]
- [CALOY GRUNTS]

15
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:50,550
[BILLY] No!

16
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:53,094
[GRUNTS] <i>Mariela, no!</i>

17
00:00:53,178 --> 00:00:55,722
- [BILLY WHIMPERING]
- [MARIELA GRUNTING]

18
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:56,681
<i>No!</i>

19
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:00,143
[BILLY WHIMPERS]

20
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:05,440
<i>You're the bane of our existence.</i>

21
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:07,692
<i>Did you know that!?</i>

22
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:09,986
- [BILLY WHIMPERS]
<i>- Pull the trigger.</i>

23
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:12,322
- [CALOY GRUNTS]
- [BILLY YELPS]

24
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:13,364
[GUNSHOT]

25
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:16,034
[BILLY BREATHING RAGGEDLY IN FEAR]

26
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:23,792
<i>Caloy. </i>[BREATHING RAGGEDLY]

27
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:25,168
<i>Caloy, you need to go to the hospital.</i>

28
00:01:26,669 --> 00:01:28,463
<i>Caloy, you need treatment!</i>

29
00:01:28,546 --> 00:01:30,757
<i>- I'm okay.</i>
<i>- No! You're not okay!</i>

30
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:32,717
<i>We need to go to the hospital!</i>

31
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:34,886
<i>- Caloy!</i>
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

32
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:35,929
<i>Caloy!</i>

33
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:37,514
<i>Caloy…</i>

34
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:39,140
[GASPS]

35
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:40,683
[BEA] <i>Caloy.</i>

36
00:01:42,352 --> 00:01:43,269
<i>Caloy.</i>

37
00:01:43,353 --> 00:01:47,524
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

38
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:48,858
<i>Caloy.</i>

39
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:54,864
<i>'Bi…</i>

40
00:01:56,699 --> 00:01:57,617
<i>Help me.</i>

41
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,410
<i>I don't want to die.</i>

42
00:02:00,328 --> 00:02:02,622
<i>Die? What do you mean?</i>

43
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:04,499
<i>No one's going to die.</i>

44
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:06,000
<i>You're not going to die!</i>

45
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:08,503
<i>- You can't die.</i>
<i>- I don't want to.</i>

46
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:09,921
<i>You made a promise to me!</i>

47
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:12,298
<i>Weren't you going to take me</i>
<i>somewhere far away?</i>

48
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:14,884
<i>You were going to help me</i>
<i>and my mother escape, right?</i>

49
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:17,846
<i>So you're not allowed to die!</i>
<i>N-No one's going to die!</i>

50
00:02:17,929 --> 00:02:20,974
<i>If I survive…</i>

51
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:24,894
<i>I'll fix everything.</i>

52
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:26,938
<i>Y-Yes, yes…</i>

53
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:29,274
<i>- I'll change.</i>
<i>- You're going to live.</i>

54
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:31,025
[STAMMERS] <i>We'll turn our lives around.</i>

55
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:34,863
<i>- It'll be a new day, Caloy.</i>
- [CALOY] <i>For you.</i>

56
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:39,367
[BEA] <i>Yes, and then we'll go far away.</i>
<i>We'll live a peaceful life.</i>

57
00:02:39,450 --> 00:02:42,412
[CALOY]<i> For the family</i>
<i>we're going to have.</i>

58
00:02:42,495 --> 00:02:44,414
[BEA] <i>We'll do that.</i>
<i>We'll make it come true, Caloy.</i>

59
00:02:44,497 --> 00:02:46,249
<i>No one's going to die, okay?</i>

60
00:02:46,332 --> 00:02:48,126
<i>No one's going to die! You can't leave me!</i>

61
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:49,836
<i>No one's going to die!</i>

62
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,757
<i>Bea hasn't returned to the apartment.</i>

63
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:56,926
<i>Do you think something</i>
<i>happened to your sister?</i>

64
00:02:58,136 --> 00:02:59,596
<i>What do you think, Dad?</i>

65
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:03,016
<i>She's probably gone into hiding</i>
<i>with Mariela!</i>

66
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:05,768
<i>I just hoped she might've changed.</i>

67
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:08,021
<i>You don't even know Bea, Dad!</i>

68
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:10,481
<i>You don't even know me!</i>

69
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:12,692
<i>How could you possibly know</i>
<i>your own children?</i>

70
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:14,235
<i>You abandoned us, didn't you?</i>

71
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:17,780
<i>And now you want to act like</i>
<i>a father to all three of us?</i>

72
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:24,412
<i>Stop believing that woman!</i>
<i>We're all suffering because of her!</i>

73
00:03:24,495 --> 00:03:25,622
<i>Billy!</i>

74
00:03:26,706 --> 00:03:28,374
<i>Why are you mad at Papa?!</i>

75
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:43,306
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:44,784
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

77
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:51,124
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:16,733
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:05:19,569 --> 00:05:22,697
<i>If I survive…</i>

80
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:26,451
<i>I'll fix everything.</i>

81
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:28,786
<i>Y-Yes, yes…</i>

82
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:31,205
<i>- I'll change.</i>
<i>- You're going to live.</i>

83
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:33,166
[STAMMERS] <i>We'll turn our lives around.</i>

84
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:37,045
<i>- It'll be a new day, Caloy.</i>
<i>- For you.</i>

85
00:05:37,962 --> 00:05:41,424
[BEA] <i>Yes, and then we'll go far away.</i>
<i>We'll live a peaceful life.</i>

86
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:44,469
<i>For the family we're going to have.</i>

87
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:46,220
<i>We'll do that.</i>
<i>We'll make it come true, Caloy.</i>

88
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:48,222
<i>No one's going to die, okay?</i>

89
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:49,891
<i>No one's going to die! You can't leave me!</i>

90
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:51,559
<i>No one's going to die!</i>

91
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:52,769
<i>Bea…</i>

92
00:05:52,852 --> 00:05:55,104
[BEA SOBBING]

93
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:57,899
<i>I love you. I love you so much.</i>

94
00:05:57,982 --> 00:06:00,902
[SOBS] <i>I love you too! I love you too!</i>

95
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:03,071
<i>I love you so much!</i>

96
00:06:03,154 --> 00:06:05,239
<i>That's why you can't die!</i>

97
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:07,492
<i>Caloy! Caloy!</i>

98
00:06:07,575 --> 00:06:14,248
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES THEN FADES]

99
00:06:14,332 --> 00:06:20,296
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

100
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:57,708
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

101
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:28,072
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

102
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:39,834
[BEA] <i>Please forgive me…</i>

103
00:07:41,752 --> 00:07:44,338
<i>for everything I've done wrong.</i>

104
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:50,553
<i>If it wasn't for me…</i>

105
00:07:53,014 --> 00:07:56,767
<i>the man who truly loved me</i>
<i>would've still been alive.</i>

106
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:59,479
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

107
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:03,149
[CRYING] <i>I hope you can also</i>
<i>forgive my mother.</i>

108
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:10,698
<i>Please protect her wherever she is.</i>

109
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:15,495
<i>I promise I'll change for the better.</i>

110
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,748
<i>I'm going to do the right thing.</i>

111
00:08:20,124 --> 00:08:22,126
<i>I was wrong.</i>

112
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:25,671
<i>I regret everything I've done.</i>

113
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:28,174
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

114
00:08:28,257 --> 00:08:29,467
[SNIFFLES]

115
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:33,387
<i>Please forgive me. I'm really sorry.</i>

116
00:08:33,471 --> 00:08:40,144
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

117
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:51,030
[MUSIC FADES]

118
00:08:51,113 --> 00:08:56,452
DON'T WORRY.
I'M KEEPING AN EYE ON YOUR BROTHER.

119
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:57,620
[PHONE THUDS]

120
00:08:59,163 --> 00:09:06,170
[OBJECTS RUSTLING]

121
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,423
Billy?

122
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:13,844
I know you're angry about what happened.

123
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:16,722
But please don't take it out
on your father.

124
00:09:17,598 --> 00:09:19,725
You know his condition.

125
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:23,521
Can you blame me, Auntie?

126
00:09:25,481 --> 00:09:27,733
Am I always the one
who has to understand everyone else?

127
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:32,113
Billy, I understand how you feel.

128
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:34,490
But what's done is done.

129
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:37,868
Let's just be thankful
that we're all safe.

130
00:09:39,495 --> 00:09:40,663
For how long?

131
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:47,044
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

132
00:09:57,888 --> 00:10:00,975
[MUSIC FADES]

133
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:12,278
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

134
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:34,091
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:38,554
[BEA] Ma. Ma?

136
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:45,144
- Bea?
- Ma.

137
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:46,270
[MARIELA] Dear…

138
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:51,025
- Bea.
- Oh.

139
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:03,454
Caloy's death…

140
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:05,748
That was Billy's fault.

141
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:09,001
You asked her to help
clear my name, right?

142
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,628
Did she grant your request?

143
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:12,046
No.

144
00:11:12,129 --> 00:11:15,883
That's why you had to ask Caloy for help.

145
00:11:15,966 --> 00:11:19,512
And when he was about to get me out,
that Billy interfered.

146
00:11:20,429 --> 00:11:25,684
So Billy's the reason Caloy died.

147
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:27,728
Let's make her pay.

148
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,897
Let's make them all pay.

149
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:36,779
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

150
00:11:40,616 --> 00:11:44,495
Your sister is mad at me
because I didn't believe her right away.

151
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:48,582
So don't be upset with your sister.
I'm in the wrong here.

152
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:53,712
Pa, is Bea a bad person?

153
00:11:55,464 --> 00:11:58,134
Bea has made a lot of mistakes.

154
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:03,931
Billy said that if I see Bea,

155
00:12:05,182 --> 00:12:07,101
I should avoid her

156
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:09,728
and inform Billy right away.

157
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:14,316
She also said Bea is wanted by the cops,

158
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,277
along with her mother.

159
00:12:18,112 --> 00:12:19,530
Just remember this:

160
00:12:20,531 --> 00:12:22,992
Bea won't hurt you.

161
00:12:24,952 --> 00:12:28,497
What about her mother, Pa?

162
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,419
I'll protect you, son.

163
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:34,462
Okay.

164
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,256
Sure.

165
00:12:37,339 --> 00:12:38,799
- Here's your bag.
- Okay.

166
00:12:38,883 --> 00:12:40,301
- Take care.
- I will.

167
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:41,469
Bye-bye!

168
00:12:45,347 --> 00:12:46,765
[CELLPHONE RINGS]

169
00:12:49,101 --> 00:12:50,352
Hello, Bea?

170
00:12:51,937 --> 00:12:52,897
Where are you?

171
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:56,984
I'm at the Holy Family Church.

172
00:12:58,402 --> 00:13:00,446
- Are you with your mother?
<i>- Pa…</i>

173
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:03,324
Pa, I'm sorry. Billy is right.

174
00:13:05,075 --> 00:13:06,577
Pa, I'm turning myself in.

175
00:13:07,161 --> 00:13:10,623
I'll also surrender Mama
if it'll bring peace to everyone.

176
00:13:13,292 --> 00:13:14,376
Pa…

177
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:18,214
- Pa, I'm really sorry.
- You traitor!

178
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:19,924
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

179
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:24,929
You promised I'd be free,
and now you're taking it back?

180
00:13:25,012 --> 00:13:26,889
Bea? Bea!

181
00:13:26,972 --> 00:13:29,058
- I won't let you!
- [BODY THUDS]

182
00:13:29,141 --> 00:13:30,309
Ma!

183
00:13:30,392 --> 00:13:33,896
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:13:33,979 --> 00:13:35,105
Ma!

185
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:37,107
Ma!

186
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:38,442
Bea!

187
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:40,152
[GRUNTS]

188
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:44,365
Ma!

189
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:49,995
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:51,288
[MUSIC FADES]

191
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:53,457
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

192
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:56,794
<i>Before we discovered LoveList,</i>
<i>we almost gave up on love.</i>

193
00:13:56,877 --> 00:13:58,963
<i>Fortunately, we made the right choice.</i>

194
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:00,506
<i>We gave love a second chance.</i>

195
00:14:00,589 --> 00:14:02,758
<i>Because of LoveList,</i>

196
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:04,843
<i>you too will find your forever.</i>

197
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:07,137
<i>And will live happily ever after</i>

198
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:08,597
<i>with the right one</i>

199
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:10,182
<i>at the right time.</i>

200
00:14:10,266 --> 00:14:13,394
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:15,396
<i>Didn't I tell you before?</i>

202
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:16,605
<i>But you didn't listen!</i>

203
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:18,857
<i>You believed your eldest instead.</i>

204
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:20,359
<i>It's my fault too.</i>

205
00:14:20,442 --> 00:14:22,862
<i>I shouldn't have kept giving in</i>
<i>to what you wanted.</i>

206
00:14:24,446 --> 00:14:26,866
<i>I just hoped she might've changed.</i>

207
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:29,159
<i>You don't even know Bea, Dad!</i>

208
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:31,620
<i>You don't even know me!</i>

209
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:33,831
<i>How could you possibly know</i>
<i>your own children?</i>

210
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:35,374
<i>You abandoned us, didn't you?</i>

211
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:40,921
<i>And now you want to act like</i>
<i>a father to all three of us?</i>

212
00:14:43,007 --> 00:14:47,052
<i>Stop believing that woman!</i>
<i>We're all suffering because of her!</i>

213
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:48,721
<i>Billy!</i>

214
00:14:49,805 --> 00:14:51,473
<i>Why are you mad at Papa?!</i>

215
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:52,892
<i>Oliver…</i>

216
00:14:54,351 --> 00:14:56,020
<i>It's my fault.</i>

217
00:14:57,521 --> 00:15:04,361
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

218
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:06,196
Chief?

219
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,490
[MUSIC STOPS]

220
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:16,040
So what exactly are we trying
to achieve with this?

221
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:17,708
Uh…

222
00:15:17,791 --> 00:15:21,295
So, we tried hitting two birds
with one stone, chief.

223
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:23,672
We featured
the success stories of LoveList

224
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:26,050
and The Happily Ever After couple.

225
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:30,095
And then, we also showcased
a Filipina and foreigner couple

226
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:32,014
because it's trending right now.

227
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:34,892
They actually call it
the "Better Life" love stories.

228
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:36,560
It's messy.

229
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:38,395
There is no impact or focus.

230
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:40,773
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

231
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:42,816
Why did you upload this
without my consent?

232
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,319
Look at the comments.

233
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:47,947
Look at it!

234
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:50,366
Here.

235
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:56,246
"LoveList? More like HateList.
You never run out of issues."

236
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,707
"Your CEO is on the news again."

237
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:01,919
Clearly, this video campaign
you posted isn't enough

238
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:04,171
to redirect these hate comments.

239
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:07,091
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

240
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:08,217
Look!

241
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:11,845
Our subscription rate is declining!

242
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:14,098
[CHARM] Hmm…

243
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:18,435
Do you think
a free subscription promo will work?

244
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:22,940
[TONI] Maybe.

245
00:16:23,023 --> 00:16:26,777
But since our budget is very limited,

246
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:30,906
we can limit it to just three months.

247
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:36,245
We can also offer loyalty rewards
for long-term users

248
00:16:36,328 --> 00:16:40,207
or subscription discounts for referrals.

249
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:42,376
Discounts?

250
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:45,587
The company is bleeding money
and you'll offer discounts?

251
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:48,716
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

252
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:51,885
DOES LOVELIST HAVE ANYTHING TO OFFER
BESIDES HEADACHES?

253
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:54,388
Uh…

254
00:16:54,471 --> 00:16:55,639
Chief…

255
00:16:55,723 --> 00:16:57,641
It's… It's a scheme.

256
00:16:57,725 --> 00:17:00,060
I know it's a scheme, Marj!
I'm not stupid!

257
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:02,396
My point is, you didn't inform me again.

258
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:09,319
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

259
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:28,714
WILL INSTALL THE APP
IF I'LL MATCH WITH JORDAN!

260
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:31,550
LEAVE LOVELIST, IDOL.
BEFORE THEY DRAG YOU DOWN.

261
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:38,223
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

262
00:17:47,357 --> 00:17:48,859
Hi, chief!

263
00:17:48,942 --> 00:17:50,694
This came in the mail for you.

264
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:08,462
Uh, chief? Would you like some coffee?

265
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:12,716
[GRUNTING]

266
00:18:14,384 --> 00:18:16,762
Ugh! Seriously?!

267
00:18:16,845 --> 00:18:22,810
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

268
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:29,900
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

269
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:39,701
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

270
00:18:55,008 --> 00:18:56,343
[CELLPHONE RINGS]

271
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:57,928
<i>Enrico?</i>

272
00:18:58,011 --> 00:18:59,138
<i>Hello, Precious?</i>

273
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:03,934
<i>Uh… I've been trying to reach you.</i>

274
00:19:04,017 --> 00:19:05,853
<i>Are you and Oliver home?</i>

275
00:19:05,936 --> 00:19:07,604
<i>Yes, we're home.</i>

276
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,857
<i>Why? Is there a problem?</i>

277
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:12,276
<i>Just be vigilant.</i>

278
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:14,820
<i>Watch out for Mariela.</i>

279
00:19:14,903 --> 00:19:15,821
<i>What?!</i>

280
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:22,995
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

281
00:19:36,508 --> 00:19:37,843
<i>Are you on your way home?</i>

282
00:19:37,926 --> 00:19:38,927
<i>Your father called.</i>

283
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:40,721
<i>He said we should look out for Mariela.</i>

284
00:19:40,804 --> 00:19:42,639
[LOCKS RATTLING]

285
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:45,601
<i>She might come for us here.</i>

286
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:47,603
<i>What?!</i>

287
00:19:47,686 --> 00:19:49,646
<i>Auntie, how does he know that?</i>

288
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,565
<i>I didn't get to ask him.</i>

289
00:19:51,648 --> 00:19:54,610
<i>He said he already called the police,</i>

290
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:56,361
<i>but they aren't here yet.</i>

291
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:01,742
<i>A-Are you Bea's mother?</i>

292
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:03,744
<i>P-Please let me go!</i>

293
00:20:03,827 --> 00:20:05,120
<i>Where do you think you're going?</i>

294
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,122
<i>- You're gonna tell on me?</i>
- [GRUNTS]

295
00:20:07,706 --> 00:20:09,041
<i>Your old house burned down,</i>

296
00:20:09,124 --> 00:20:11,084
<i>yet you still have a nice place to live.</i>

297
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:15,589
<i>When that happened to us,</i>
<i>we were left with nothing!</i>

298
00:20:15,672 --> 00:20:18,884
<i>I only want my husband back,</i>

299
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:21,887
<i>but I can't have him because of you!</i>

300
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:22,804
[GLASS SHATTERS]

301
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:24,556
<i>Please calm down, Mariela.</i>

302
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:27,351
<i>Calm down and let's talk</i>
<i>about this properly.</i>

303
00:20:27,434 --> 00:20:30,062
<i>We have nothing to talk about.</i>

304
00:20:30,145 --> 00:20:33,440
- [OLIVER GRUNTS]
<i>- I will kill you all!</i>

305
00:20:33,523 --> 00:20:35,901
<i>No, Mariela! Don't drag Oliver into this!</i>

306
00:20:35,984 --> 00:20:37,361
<i>Don't hurt him, please!</i>

307
00:20:37,444 --> 00:20:40,948
<i>To hell with all of you!</i>
<i>I'll spare no one!</i>

308
00:20:41,031 --> 00:20:44,076
<i>I'll erase you from our lives for good!</i>

309
00:20:44,159 --> 00:20:45,494
<i>- Let him go-- Ah!</i>
- [SCREAMING]

310
00:20:45,577 --> 00:20:48,497
- [FLESH RIPS]
<i>- Ah! </i>[EXCLAIMS]

311
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:49,915
<i>- Bea? Bea!</i>
- [WHIMPERING]

312
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:51,959
<i>Ugh!</i>

313
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:55,420
[SCREAMING] <i>This is your fault, Oliver!</i>

314
00:20:56,296 --> 00:20:58,173
<i>No! Oliver!</i>

315
00:20:58,257 --> 00:20:59,258
<i>Pa?</i>

316
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:00,217
<i>Ah…</i>

317
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:02,427
- <i>Ah!</i>
- <i>Pa.</i>

318
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:04,346
<i>Pa!</i>

319
00:21:04,888 --> 00:21:06,265
<i>- Pa! Pa!</i>
- [ENRICO GROANS]

320
00:21:07,224 --> 00:21:08,183
[ENRICO WHIMPERS]

321
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:09,476
<i>Pa!</i>

322
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:15,148
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]
